st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.


wm development configuration
----------------------------
This checkout is not installed or activated. Validate from the parent wm
repository with make test. Do not run the installation commands below during
this preparation phase.

The wm profile uses Hack Nerd Font Mono at 11 points as its only primary font,
the existing Alacritty palette, zero fixed padding, a blinking block
cursor, Ctrl+Insert copy and familiar copy/paste/zoom shortcuts. Backgrounds
are opaque by default (alpha 1.0); -A can explicitly request transparency.
No blur implementation is added to st itself; the wm compositor disables blur. Scrollback holds 2000 physical
rows, with resize reflow of the default screen/history and separate alternate
screen contents. Shift+PageUp/PageDown scrolls a page; the wheel scrolls three
rows unless the application requests mouse events (Shift overrides it).
Column changes clear the selection. OSC 52 clipboard writes are enabled, so
applications (including remote programs over SSH) can replace the system
clipboard. Set allowwindowops to 0 to disable this. Shift+mouse selection
joins terminal-wrapped rows, but keeps explicit line breaks; application-drawn
rows may not preserve the original logical line. Prefer application-owned
copying through OSC 52 for those cases.
The core is tested with ASan/UBSan and
synthetic input, not a live terminal session.

History/reflow adapts the suckless community scrollback 0.9.2 and reflow 0.9.2
patches, based on work by BeyondMagic et al. The bounded resize ring and wide
cell handling follow bakkeby/st-flexipatch (MIT/X Consortium license). Sources
and provenance are retained in the parent wm repository under patches/upstream.
Missing glyphs use st's existing Fontconfig fallback. Do not add Noto Color Emoji
to the primary family list: matching can select it for the entire terminal and
impose its bitmap strike size. Color emoji and visual rendering still need an
authorized visual test.
TERM remains st-256color; prepare matching terminfo during future installation,
including remote hosts where it is needed. Do not substitute TERM blindly.

Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.

